{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SpYyZ2wjA9FbufB1rYeeKS","type":"tool_result","content":"{\r\n  \"id\": \"US-220\",\r\n  \"title\": \"Implement Next.js 16.1 Turbopack filesystem caching for faster local dev builds\",\r\n  \"priority\": \"medium\",\r\n  \"description\": \"Next.js 16.1 (December 2025) introduced Turbopack filesystem caching for development, delivering 50%+ faster cold-start rebuild times by persisting the compilation cache across restarts. This improves developer velocity significantly on the hostel website project, which has growing page count and schema components. Enabling it requires opting in via next.config.ts.\",\r\n  \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\r\n    \"next.config.ts enables Turbopack filesystem caching via the experimental.turbopackPersistentCaching flag (or stable API when available)\",\r\n    \"Cold-start dev server time (npm run dev after cache clear) is measured before and after \\u2014 improvement of at least 30% documented\",\r\n    \"Hot reload time for a typical page (home page with schema components) is measured and confirmed \\u22642s\",\r\n    \"No build errors or cache invalidation issues occur after config changes or dependency updates\",\r\n    \"The .next/cache directory is excluded from version control but preserved between dev sessions\"\r\n  ],\r\n  \"technicalNotes\": [\r\n    \"Next.js 16.1 announcement: https://nextjs.org/blog/next-16-1\",\r\n    \"Turbopack filesystem caching opt-in: https://nextjs.org/docs/app/api-reference/turbopack\",\r\n    \"StaticMania review of 16.1: https://staticmania.com/blog/next.js-16.1-review\",\r\n    \"Install size is 20MB smaller in 16.1 due to simplified Turbopack caching layer \\u2014 also upgrade if not already on 16.1\"\r\n  ],\r\n  \"dependencies\": [],\r\n  \"estimatedComplexity\": \"small\",\r\n  \"passes\": false,\r\n  \"model\": \"sonnet\",\r\n  \"_failureReason\": \"oversized_diff: produced 1559 lines but limit is 500. Keep total insertio