{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01QJLzYNGa9DjehAco4wpyK9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Good. Next.js 16.1.6 uses `turbopackFileSystemCacheForDev` (already enabled) and `turbopackFileSystemCacheForBuild` (not yet enabled). The story's `turbopackPersistentCaching` doesn't exist — the current API IS the stable one.\n\n## Current State\n- `next.config.ts` already has `turbopackFileSystemCacheForDev: true` (from US-160) inside `experimental`\n- Next.js 16.1.6 also supports `turbopackFileSystemCacheForBuild` which is not yet enabled\n- `.next/` is already in `.gitignore`, covering `.next/cache`\n- Dev script already uses `--turbo` flag\n\n## Problem Identified\nUS-220 wants the full Turbopack filesystem caching story completed: the dev caching comment needs to reference US-220 as the completion story, and build caching should also be enabled for complete coverage. Performance needs to be verified.\n\n## Planned Changes\n- **`site/next.config.ts`**: Update comment on existing flag to reference US-220, add `turbopackFileSystemCacheForBuild: true`\n- **`prd.json`**: Mark US-220 as `passes: true`\n- **`progress.txt`**: Document implementation and measurements\n\n<plan>\n{\n  \"files_to_create\": [],\n  \"files_to_modify\": [\"site/next.config.ts\", \"prd.json\", \"progress.txt\"],\n  \"functions_to_add\": [],\n  \"estimated_loc\": 15\n}\n</plan>\n\nLet me verify the build works first, then make the minimal changes."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":155,"cache_read_input_tokens":34232,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":155},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cc0cb108-6a31-408b-bd96-18d17a736d90","uuid":"25dbfca2-09cf-4731-a09f-8f33a5120559"}
